## 16. Acceptance Criteria

The application is complete as an initial prototype when:

1. All five navigation destinations work.
2. The Home screen clearly distinguishes Start my check-in from View mood history.
3. A selected mood is passed into the demo Cara.ai conversation.
4. Cara.ai offers different next steps based on the selected response.
5. Recommended tools can be opened directly from the conversation.
6. All four wellbeing tools have functional guided interactions.
7. Workload Triage produces an editable, actionable plan.
8. The module library has distinct cards and configurable links.
9. My Wellbeing displays actual demo entries or an honest empty state.
10. Journal entries can be created, edited and deleted within the supported storage model.
11. Get Support distinguishes professional messaging, general professional resources and urgent crisis support.
12. Unimplemented integrations are clearly labelled and do not falsely claim to provide real services.
13. The interface follows the exact colour palette and feels calm, consistent and professional.
14. The application is responsive, keyboard-accessible and usable on mobile.
15. The app does not diagnose users or present Cara.ai as a replacement for professional help.

## 17. Build Priority

Build in this order:

**Phase 1 — Core interactive prototype**
- Shared design system and navigation.
- Home screen and mood check-in.
- Cara.ai branching conversation.
- At least one fully functional wellbeing exercise.
- Workload Triage.
- My Wellbeing with mood history and journal.
- Get Support with clearly labelled demo states.

**Phase 2 — Complete the experience**
- Remaining wellbeing exercises.
- Module library.
- Streaks and activity history.
- Settings and privacy controls.
- Responsive and accessibility refinements.

**Phase 3 — Production integrations**
- Live AI backend and safety controls.
- Secure data storage and authentication, if required.
- Verified professional support directory.
- Secure professional messaging.
- Real module content and source references.

Start by implementing the complete Phase 1 experience. Prioritise working interactions, consistent design and a coherent user journey over decorative effects. Make reasonable implementation decisions without removing or renaming the specified core features.
